INT. LAUNDROMAT - 2 A.M.

A buzzing sign: "OPEN 24 HRS." Rows of dryers tumble in sleepy rhythm. The floor is sticky. A TV above the folding table plays infomercials on mute.

RUBY ACHTERBERG, 17, in an oversized hoodie, sits on a dryer, legs dangling, eating gummy worms. Across from her, DOMINIC "DOMI" PELLEGRINO, 17, stands guard over a laundry bag.

RUBY
Domi, you've been folding that sock for ten minutes.

DOMI
It's a delicate operation.

KWABENA ASARE, 18, a lanky skateboarder with a broken wrist in a cast, slips through the door, board under his good arm. SHOSHANA BLUM, 17, in a prom dress and combat boots, follows two steps behind.

KWABENA
Look who's still alive.

DOMI
Kwabena. You're supposed to be at the hospital.

KWABENA
Hospital's boring. Shoshana drove.

SHOSHANA
I did not drive. I steered. Your skateboard did the rest.

RUBY
She means she dragged him on it.

SHOSHANA
Ruby, you're not helping.

Domi drops the sock. He walks up to Shoshana, close.

DOMI
Why are you wearing a prom dress at two a.m.?

SHOSHANA
Because someone asked me and then left me at the punch bowl.

Ruby slides off the dryer. Kwabena looks at his shoes.

RUBY
Kwabena. Tell me you did not.

KWABENA
I got a call about the cast, okay? I had to go!

SHOSHANA
You told me it was an emergency. It was a cast.

DOMI
You left her at prom for a cast?

KWABENA
It hurt, Domi!

Domi shoves Kwabena. Kwabena stumbles into a dryer and drops the board. Ruby grabs Domi's arm. Shoshana kicks the board away.

RUBY
Enough! All of you!

SHOSHANA
Ruby, let him hit me. I want to know what it feels like.

DOMI
I'm not hitting you!

KWABENA
Then why are you shouting?

Silence. A dryer buzzes and the door pops open. A single red sock rolls out and spins to a stop on the tile.

Ruby picks it up. She holds it out to Domi. He takes it. His hand is shaking.

DOMI
Sorry, Shosh.

SHOSHANA
Sorry, Kwabena. I did steer.

KWABENA
You steered fine.
